Summary

`JobLogController#logDetailCat` accepts a user-controlled `logId` and returns the full execution log of the corresponding job — including the executor's internal address, internal class names, stack traces, and the `executorParam` value supplied by the job owner — **without calling `JobGroupPermissionUtil.validJobGroupPermission`**.

The other four endpoints in the same controller (`pageList`, `logKill`, `clearLog`, `logDetailPage`) all perform that check. Only `logDetailCat` is missing it.

Any logged-in non-admin user can enumerate `logId` (auto-increment `long`) and read the execution logs of **every job in every job group**, including groups they are not authorized to access.

## Root Cause

`xxl-job-admin/src/main/java/com/xxl/job/admin/business/controller/JobLogController.java:295-327`

```java
@RequestMapping("/logDetailCat")
@ResponseBody
public Response<LogResult> logDetailCat(@RequestParam("logId") long logId,
