Trivial enumeration.** `logId` is an auto-increment `long`. Every historical log is reachable; reads do not write `xxl_job_log`, so there is no audit trail.
3. **Breaks the multi-tenant boundary** introduced by the `permission` field in 3.x. The whole point of granting users a subset of `jobGroup` IDs is silently defeated.
4. **Feeds other chains.** Information harvested from logs (executor addresses, executor params) can be combined with the publicly known default `xxl.job.accessToken=default_token` to drive CVE-2022-43183-class RCE on the executor side.

